CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 4 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.\d+\] line \d+ value-pack call, 1 element: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.\d+\] line \d+ value-pack call, 3 elements: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.\d+\] line \d+ value-pack forward, two layers: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.\d+\] line \d+ type-pack class-template argument, 3 elements: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.\d+\] line \d+ sizeof\.\.\.\(T\) in a member function, 3 elements: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Locks in the [temp.variadic] pack-expansion contexts CBMC already handles:
value-pack expansion in a function-call argument list (1/3 elements, forwarded
through two layers), a type pack forwarded as a class-template argument, and
sizeof...(T) in a member function body.  Guards against regressions from the
unified pack-expansion rework
(doc/architectural/cpp-variadic-pack-expansion-rework.md).
